{#-
  Cisco IOS / IOS-XE -- standard access lists.

    ip access-list standard NAME
     permit 10.1.1.0 0.0.0.255
     deny   any log

  IOS matches on a wildcard mask, so the CIDR from the standards file is
  converted by the `wildcard` filter (a /32 becomes `host 10.1.1.5`).

  The negation comes first: an ACL whose entries are in the wrong order is
  removed and written back, because there is no reordering that is safer.
-#}
{% for entry in remove %}
no {{ entry.line }}
{% endfor %}
{% for name in add %}
{% set acl = acls[name] %}
ip access-list standard {{ name }}
{% for item in acl.entries %}
 {{ item.action }} {% if item.target == 'any' %}any{% else %}{{ item.target | wildcard }}{% endif %}{% if item.log %} log{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
